/b.wf:3:5: error[W0229]: cannot infer a type for `untyped` from `null`
  |
3 | var untyped = null
  |     ^^^^^^^
  = help: annotate it: `untyped: T? = null`
/b.wf:4:5: error[W0200]: `no_init` has type `int` but no initial value
  |
4 | var no_init: int
  |     ^^^^^^^
  = help: give it one (`var no_init: int = …`), or make the type nullable (`int?`)
/b.wf:6:6: error[W0213]: parameter `p` needs a type
  |
6 | fn f(p) {
  |      ^
  = help: write `p: T`, or `p: any` to opt out of static checking
/b.wf:7:9: error[W0229]: cannot infer a type for `a` from `null`
  |
7 |     let a = null
  |         ^
  = help: annotate it: `a: T? = null`
/b.wf:9:18: error[W0263]: array elements have different types: `int` and `string` (element 2)
  |
9 |     let xs = [1, "two"]
  |                  ^^^^^
  = help: annotate the binding to allow mixed values, e.g. `let xs: [any] = …`
/b.wf:10:27: error[W0265]: map values have different types: `int` and `bool`
   |
10 |     let m = {"a": 1, "b": true}
   |                           ^^^^
   = help: annotate the binding to allow mixed values, e.g. `{string: any}`
/b.wf:11:16: error[W0264]: `[int]` cannot be a map key
   |
11 |     let bad = {[1]: 2}
   |                ^^^
   = help: map keys must be int, string, bool or object
/b.wf:12:12: error[W0222]: unknown type `objekt`
   |
12 |     let t: objekt = self
   |            ^^^^^^
   = help: did you mean `object`?

